abstract: >-
  A prototype biological dual-use content classifier built using Anthropic's
  Constitutional Classifiers methodology. Defines a 56-rule biosafety
  constitution across 7 NSABB categories, generates ~4,500 synthetic training
  examples via Claude API, and fine-tunes DeBERTa-v3-base for binary safe/unsafe
  classification. Held-out F1 = 0.980, AUROC = 0.998, 0/325 over-refusal FPR;
  9.79% mean adversarial ASR across 20 attack types. Intended as a research
  artifact, not a production safeguard.
